# omarchy-egpu system half
# omarchy-egpu-version: 0.1.3
#
# Keeps the compositor off the eGPU's card node (system/install.sh installs this
# as /etc/udev/rules.d/72-omarchy-egpu-seat.rules). It sorts after systemd's
# 71-seat.rules, which tags every DRM card "seat" and "master-of-seat"; a rule
# before it could not take those tags off again.
#
# Why: Hyprland's backend (aquamarine) reads AQ_DRM_DEVICES only for the GPUs
# present at login. A GPU that appears later is opened as a secondary device
# whatever the list says, and its fd is kept, one more per plug-in. logind keeps
# its own copy of that fd (TakeDevice) and PID 1 holds logind's (the fd store).
# The driver cannot unload while any of them is open, so a safe eject said
# "still in use: Hyprland, systemd-logind, systemd" until the next logout.
#
# What: a card node without the "seat" tag is not on any seat, so logind
# refuses TakeDevice for it and Hyprland's open fails quietly. No new seat is
# made (a seat with a master device would be offered to the display manager as
# a place for a login screen). Render nodes and /dev/nvidia* are untouched:
# apps still offload to the card. The effect starts at the next plug-in.
#
# The display policy egpu-hdmi (the compositor drives the eGPU's ports) needs
# the card on the user's seat: create /etc/omarchy-egpu/egpu-display to switch
# this off. TEST is evaluated per event, so no reload is needed.

ACTION=="remove", GOTO="omarchy_egpu_seat_end"

SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="drm_minor", SUBSYSTEMS=="pci", ATTRS{class}=="0x03[0-9]*", ATTRS{removable}=="removable", TEST!="/etc/omarchy-egpu/egpu-display", TAG-="seat", TAG-="master-of-seat"

LABEL="omarchy_egpu_seat_end"
